=== p2-windows · W7 · page:settings/TwoFactorAuth (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:settings/TwoFactorAuth   kind=page   web route=/account/2fa
Web source  : web/src/features/settings/pages/TwoFactorAuthPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/TwoFactorAuthPage/** (+ shell registration, Strings/*.resw, tests)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repo's WinUI app is code-first C# (no per-page .xaml). Every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (Microsoft.UI-free Registration / value
  types / projection / controller seam / diagnostics — unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's
  idealized "TwoFactorAuthPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Settings" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("TwoFactorAuth"), which RouteTable
  already maps to account/2fa.
- The web page is a thin PageContainer hosting <TOTPEnrollmentSection/>. Ported 1:1 as a thin TwoFactorAuthPage
  (shared PageContainer: title + subtitle + copy-link) hosting a native TotpEnrollmentSection that reproduces the
  web component's glass panel and EVERY render branch — loading / open-mode / not-enrolled / active — plus the three
  dialog flows (enroll QR + manual secret + 6-digit verify, one-time backup-codes reveal, typed-confirmation disable)
  as Fluent TsModal / TsConfirmDialog surfaces.
- Manifest models this unit as "no API data sources — renders from local state" (requiredCount=2, the two page-tier
  strings). The generated C# client (ADR-004) exposes no per-user TOTP endpoint, so the section view-model reads
  through an injected ITotpEnrollmentController whose default OpenModeTotpController resolves the open-mode notice —
  the web component's own no-backend default (the RequiresAuth-gated branch) — rather than a fabricated client call,
  mirroring the EmptyXSource → repository-backed source convention the sibling pages (QuietHours /
  BrowserNotifications) use. A host behind forward-auth injects a client-backed controller. No non-SI fields exist on
  this authentication surface, so the P1/S5 converters are N/A here.
- Pre-existing blocker repaired: ShellWindow.xaml.cs Register("Locations", …) lambda had lost its closing
  `return page; });` (a .gitattributes merge=union artifact), producing CS1026/CS1002/CS1513 at the constructor
  brace; that broke the C# compile, left the XAML MarkupCompilePass2 with no LocalAssembly (WMC1509) and cascaded
  into 84 errors (WMC9999 + every Components.UI Ts* "unknown type"). Restored the one missing close — the
  whole-solution build returns to 0 errors. Same class of merge repair the ApiLogsPage gate documented for the
  Tests csproj.
- Strings: the section's settings.totp.* keys (35) already exist in Strings/*.resw; the two page-tier keys were
  absent (not in the web i18n source — only TSX inline fallbacks), so account.twoFactor.title/subtitle were added to
  Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw as translation.account.twoFactor.* (the translation.{web-key} convention the
  sibling pages use). Every label resolves through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names; the four
  Microsoft.UI-free sources are Compile-linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests for headless coverage.

